  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute rises in military/security tensions (e.g., Taiwan strait incidents or South China Sea confrontations) prompt market-makers and principal liquidity providers to pull back, widen quoted spreads and raise internal risk limits, materially reducing depth and increasing execution costs.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
