  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher average autonomy in deployed models reduces operator workload and enables more reliable autonomous targeting, swarming, and sortie management, which militaries accelerate to increase drone operational tempo and deployment rates in the Russia–Ukraine theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_ai_governance</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_ai_governance::model_autonomy_level" target="us_china_rivalry::security_tension_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A demonstrable rise in deployed AI autonomy narrows decision cycles and increases misperception risk, prompting defensive measures (e.g., tighter rules of engagement, deployment of countermeasures) that elevate strategic-security tensions between the two powers.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_ai_governance</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
