<edge source="global_bond_stress::market_liquidity" target="russia_ukraine_war::oil_export_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Improved market liquidity reduces trade‑finance and commodity‑hedging costs and makes it easier to roll financing for tankers and traders, increasing the likelihood that crude and product cargoes are shipped on schedule and raising realized export flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_stress::market_liquidity" target="us_china_rivalry::regulatory_uncertainty" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp deterioration in market liquidity produces large, disorderly price moves in cross-border positions and prompts authorities to introduce emergency trading rules, reporting requirements or capital-flow measures directed at foreign/strategic investments, increasing regulatory unpredictability in the US–China policy space.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
