  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sharp deterioration in market liquidity increases the likelihood that any military flare-up will trigger outsized asset-price dislocations and funding stress, which incentivizes US policymakers and regional actors to avoid kinetic actions and therefore lowers near-term perceptions of imminent escalation.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_standoff</data>
